    "His October moments were larger than his season totals. The 1969 NLCS home run helped push the Mets into the World Series, and his two homers in the 1973 World Series gave an injured club more offense than it was supposed to have. Garrett was the kind of player who could be quiet for a few innings and then change a series with one swing.",
